            <ArticleTitle>Chronic abdominal pain in children: an update.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>69-75; quiz 75-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Despite the fact that chronic abdominal pain is a common complaint in children and adolescents, the complexity of this condition only recently has begun to be understood. This article summarizes new advances in the diagnosis, conceptualization, and treatment of chronic abdominal pain. Implications for effective assessment and treatment within the pediatric primary care setting are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
